{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-projective-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:936650ab3283af29c99665e39f113ad97cf6c0b7b0604a3238036c4b90a33e61", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:330672993f11c3bff8041009d5e93bd4ea0bc54e098ea6fcebf4317a9bd04ee8", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0003> is projective and <MATH_0004> is separated,\nthen <MATH_0005> is projective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:98d1866a6b3d32422e79654e0abb53d8f5c139def1c433e29dc3ddc4be7ce5dd", "unit_id": "tag:0C4Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to \\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to \\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nX \\to X \\times_S Y \\to \\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\times_S Y\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$g$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathbf{P}(g^*\\mathcal{E})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-semi-diagonal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d231802f5a00359f21332bb4ab6fd4ca992511bca791c25f7bfa59725f69e425", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0919491abd001ef4516aeffd6b061d6d4cecbada2c06acfc192323893cb6aef3", "source_text": "Choose a closed immersion <MATH_0001> where <MATH_0002>\nis a quasi-coherent, finite type <MATH_0003>-module. Then\nwe get a morphism <MATH_0004>.\nThis morphism is a closed immersion because it is the composition\n<MATH_0005>\nwhere the first morphism is a closed immersion by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>\n(and the fact that <MATH_0006> is separated) and\nthe second as the base change of a closed immersion.\nFinally, the fibre product <MATH_0007>\nis isomorphic to <MATH_0008> and pullback\npreserves quasi-coherent, finite type modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7891411e22c1d96b357ee760d8df7a21ea4ee5a1cfb191d2136ac4d55974e5b", "unit_id": "tag:0C4Q:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-projective-over-quasi-projective-is-H-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ec52e7dcca6f066005dbd6944846e97d169322dd88698a14eac5633c5c1fae7b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca13ac2a5f68e726df25df872dea3dc849676a86f0123dec96567a419160caf7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme which admits an ample invertible sheaf. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> any projective morphism <MATH_0002> is H-projective, and\n<STRUCT_0003> any quasi-projective morphism <MATH_0003> is H-quasi-projective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3eaf8c26616143f9a2f1866c51ab881c2bd4e941ca6a60a6473740dc7e3ef9af", "unit_id": "tag:087S:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_S^{\\oplus n} \\to \\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) \\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{O}_S^{\\oplus n}) = \\mathbf{P}^{n - 1}_S\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$n$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_S} \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E}) =\n\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E} \\otimes_{\\mathcal{O}_S} \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-definition-ample}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-ample-immersion-into-proj}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-proj-separated}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-projective-open-projective}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{properties-proposition-characterize-ample}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-twisting-and-proj}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e10e3c9a2b9d99260f654397810c14a8fb3d04359d5d30044b21b89075da8754", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:81296b755907b9a9231e86f73c2f8340a0c226d911a11a28a000780b4f4545c7", "source_text": "The assumptions on <MATH_0001> imply that <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact and separated, see\nProperties, Definition <REF_0001> and\nLemma <REF_0002>\nand Constructions, Lemma <REF_0003>.\nHence Lemma <REF_0004>\napplies and we see that (1) implies (2).\nLet <MATH_0003> be a finite type quasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-module.\nBy our definition of projective morphisms it suffices to show that\n<MATH_0005> is H-projective.\nIf <MATH_0006> is generated by finitely many global sections,\nthen the corresponding surjection <MATH_0007>\ninduces a closed immersion\n<MATH_0008>\nas desired. In general, let <MATH_0009> be an ample invertible sheaf on <MATH_0010>.\nBy Properties, Proposition <REF_0005>\nthere exists an integer <MATH_0011> such that\n<MATH_0012>\nis globally generated by finitely many sections. Since\n<MATH_0013> by\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0006>\nthis finishes the proof.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:79bbcb8337a649eac18bd576422ff0c3bc58946f7ea8def88ca854f482dc4844", "unit_id": "tag:087S:proof"}
